A||N||12||DaRkLoRD||ATTN: Fieroshop, Fierodave, Tom, SuperX & other Fiero business owners...||||4||
Z||000000||DaRkLoRD||06-01-2000||07:09 PM||||(I wasn't sure if this offer should go in the Mall or not, so please email me privately about this idea if you're interested!)<P>When I first asked if anyone wanted me to send them a few of my business cards, I wasn't expecting much of a response. I've given cards to a few Forum members already, and they seemed to like them.. but there were quite a few people interested in getting cards.<BR>So, I've decided to print up about a thousand of them.. I figure that'll last me a LONG time.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Anyway, Monkeyman had a great idea that would benefit a lot of people.. offer space on the backs of the cards for advertising! I have room for a few names & phone numbers or web addresses on the back of each card.. the new cards are being printed at 300dpi, so the text isn't fuzzy at all.<P>If you have a Fiero business, and would like to have your business name and contact info on the back of the cards.. email me at:  <A HREF="mailto:steve@digitalfusion.on.ca">steve@digitalfusion.on.ca</A> <P>I have room for probably 10 businesses listed.. anything more than that and it would be crowded. The idea behind the cards is to let people know where they can find lots of Fiero resources, and having businesses listed on the back of the card would be an even bigger help. These cards are going all over north america, and a few are going to Europe.. so it'd be very cheap advertising...<P>thanks for your time!!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>p.s. the first link listed on each card will be the Forum of course!||||reg||4
Z||000001||87ECO5||06-01-2000||07:55 PM||||GREAT IDEA, Steve (and Dave)!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000002||DaRkLoRD||06-01-2000||08:21 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fieroproject.com/misc/newfpcard.jpg"> <P>That's what I have for the new card design.. the top left corner is the back end of DXR_DAD's car.. the lower left is FieroGT's interior, showing the leather trans-am seats, and the main photo is an 84 SE belonging to (I believe..) Roy.<P>Before I print these.. is it ok with the owners of these photos to use these pics?||||reg||10
Z||000003||DXR_DAD||06-01-2000||08:52 PM||||We've been mixin it up for sometime now, so I'll let you know that I feel like I'm a part of "THE FIERO PROJECT" You have done some really cool stuff for me (thanks) <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"> so with that,  By all means use any and all the photos you want!!<P>DXR_DAD||||reg||6
Z||000004||Robert||06-02-2000||12:28 AM||||Hey Steve:<P>I like your idea, how about giving my company a chance to do the printing?  I could do the card on our Doc 12 digital copier or use one of our Heidelberg offset printing presses.  Take a look at my personal web site for the digital printing  <A HREF="http://www.canterburytrails.com/page6.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.canterburytrails.com/page6.html</A>   or if you would like I could send you a quote for offset printing.  I know I can do the job for less than anyone, …like the car dealers say, “ If we can’t beat the competitions price, we’ll give you the car”.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Robert<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||DaRkLoRD||06-02-2000||02:55 AM||||I've tried to reply to this twice now.. the first time, just before I hit submit a transformer was hit by lightning and the power was out for a while.. then when it came back on and I turned on my computer again, it was acting funny and I couldn't get to the reply page.. so here goes again!<BR>(note to self.. don't have computer online during a thunderstorm)<P>Actually, I have access to one as well..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>My company's business cards were printed on a Heidelberg printer.. very good quality. but they fall apart when they get wet.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>Which isn't the best thing when you're making cards designed to be left on windshields, often in the rain...<P>Anyway, thanks for your offer.. but after testing 3 different ideas, I've found that printing the cards myself on my home printer, and getting them laminated is the most cost-effective solution, as well as the best choice for durability.. my business cards fell apart when I got them wet with a spray bottle.. whereas the laminated ones could be fully submerged in water and they didn't even smudge! I doubt the cards would need to be that durable however, because if your windshield is completely under water.... a wet business card is the least of your worries.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||phillip||06-02-2000||03:12 AM||||when this subject came up a few days back  i think it was a tangent off another subject and i couldn't remember what it was. darklord, i offered to paypal you a few bucks to off set the cost. my offer still stands but i couldn't check to see if you were interested since i couldn't remember which post it was. just in case it seems like i made an offer ,then ran and hid.||||reg||1
Z||000007||fierodave||06-02-2000||05:24 AM||||Super idea  I like it!<BR>let me know what you need!<BR>FD||||reg||1
Z||000008||Monkeyman||06-02-2000||10:06 AM||||Speaking of wet cards...Glad makes some 1/2 size Ziploc plastic baggies.  They are fairly cheap.  Since I'm not allowed to carry the money (one of my wifes better ideas <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">) I'm not sure exactly what they cost, but she said they were cheaper than the regular bags.  Seems to me everyone could carry a few of these in their glovebox/map pocket/under the seat to use when putting any business card on someone elses windshield.  Just a thought.||||reg||1
Z||000009||DaRkLoRD||06-02-2000||03:07 PM||||Just as I was going to sleep last night around 5am (I work nights. heh) I remembered I didn't actually say what would be on the back of the cards!<P>I've decided that instead of having up to 10 people listed on the back, I'm going to have 5-6 businesses, and they each get 2 lines..<P>The first line would have their name, address and a couple of words to describe their business. eg. used parts.. aftermarket accessories.. etc.<BR>The second line would have their phone number and web/email address..<P>Sorry for not mentioning that before.. it slipped my mind.. (which, for those of you that know me, isn't too uncommon.. hehehe  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)||||reg||1
